<header class="page-hero" data-od-id="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Contact</span>
    <h1 class="blur-target">Tell us where you want to grow.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Send a short message and someone from OneForce will follow up — no automated sales sequence, just a real conversation about your market and your roadmap.</p>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="chapter" data-od-id="contact-main">
  <div class="wrap contact-grid">
    <div class="glass contact-card">
      <form id="contact-form" novalidate>
        <div class="form-field">
          <label for="f-name">Name</label>
          <input type="text" id="f-name" name="name" placeholder="Jordan Lee" autocomplete="name" />
          <p class="form-error">Please enter your name.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="form-field">
          <label for="f-email">Work email</label>
          <input type="email" id="f-email" name="email" placeholder="jordan@company.com" autocomplete="email" />
          <p class="form-error">Please enter a valid email address.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="form-field">
          <label for="f-company">Company <span style="color:var(--muted); font-weight:400;">(optional)</span></label>
          <input type="text" id="f-company" name="company" placeholder="Company, Inc." autocomplete="organization" />
        </div>
        <div class="form-field">
          <label for="f-message">What are you looking to solve?</label>
          <textarea id="f-message" name="message" placeholder="Tell us about your market, your team, or the growth problem you're facing."></textarea>
          <p class="form-error">Tell us a little more — a sentence or two is enough.</p>
        </div>
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-gold">Send message</button>
        <p class="form-note">We typically reply within one business day.</p>
        <div class="form-status" id="form-status"></div>
      </form>
    </div>

    <aside class="glass info-card">
      <h3>Office</h3>
      <p class="addr">10900 NE 4th St, Unit 2300<br />Bellevue, WA 98004</p>
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <div class="row"><span class="k">LinkedIn</span><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/oneforceinc/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@oneforceinc</a></div>
      <div class="row"><span class="k">Phone</span><span style="color:var(--muted);">Coming soon</span></div>
      <div class="row"><span class="k">Email</span><span style="color:var(--muted);">Coming soon</span></div>
      <div class="events-note">
        <strong>Events</strong><br />
        OneForce hosts events promoted on Luma, with relevant sessions recommended to each visitor. Listings launch here shortly — check back or follow us on LinkedIn.
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="chapter tight" data-od-id="faq">
  <div class="wrap" style="max-width: 820px;">
    <span class="eyebrow">FAQ</span>
    <h2 class="blur-target" style="margin-top: 16px; font-size: clamp(28px, 3.4vw, 40px);">Before you reach out.</h2>
    <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top: 36px;">
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What size company do you typically work with?</summary>
        <p>Most engagements are with mid-market and enterprise companies in roughly the $100M–$1B revenue range — often technology services businesses, though we work across industries with companies that are technology-literate and ready to adopt agentic AI.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Do you only do strategy, or do you also build?</summary>
        <p>Both. We prioritize an AI-adoption roadmap by impact and ROI, then can drive the transformation ourselves and build custom solutions where warranted.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>How is OneForce different from a typical AI consultancy?</summary>
        <p>We combine transformation-level business dialogue with deep technical roots — the team has enterprise IT-deployment and product-engineering backgrounds from companies like Apple, Microsoft, HP, Intel, and Amazon, plus serial-entrepreneurship experience scaling startups past $100M in revenue.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

